# Sutich Stack HA – Privacy Policy

Last updated: November 20, 2026

Sutich Stack HA is a private, single-user application. It is a personal
Home Assistant installation that connects to the owner's own Google
account (Google Calendar and Google Tasks) so the owner can see their
own events and to-do items inside their own smart home.

## What data the app accesses
- Calendar events and Tasks items belonging to the account owner, read
  through the Google Calendar and Google Tasks APIs.

## How the data is used
- It is displayed and used for automations inside the owner's private
  Home Assistant instance, running on hardware the owner controls.
- It is not sold, shared, or disclosed to any third party.
- It is not used for advertising, analytics, or profiling.

## Storage and retention
- The app keeps only the OAuth tokens needed to stay connected, stored
  locally on the owner's own Home Assistant server.
- No Google user data is copied to any external service.
- Access can be revoked at any time at
  https://myaccount.google.com/permissions

